### JavaScript (in script.js file)

```javascript
// script.js

// Get the navigation bar and footer elements
const navBar = document.getElementById('nav-bar');
const footer = document.getElementById('footer');

// Add event listener to toggle navigation bar on smaller screens
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const toggleNav = () => {
        navBar.classList.toggle('open');
    };

    // Toggle navigation bar on click
    navBar.addEventListener('click', toggleNav);

    // Toggle navigation bar on resize
    window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
        if (window.innerWidth > 768) {
            navBar.classList.remove('open');
        }
    });
});
```

This code creates a basic navigation bar and footer with JavaScript functionality to toggle the navigation bar on smaller screens. The navigation bar is fixed to the top of the page on smaller screens, and the footer is fixed to the bottom of the page. The JavaScript code uses the `DOMContentLoaded` event to ensure that the navigation bar and footer elements are available before attempting to access them. The `toggleNav` function is called when the navigation bar is clicked, and the `resize` event is used to toggle the navigation bar on resize.

